Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant tables / columns and their possible usage  

• genre.movie_id: to link each genre record to a specific movie  
• genre.genre: to know the textual genre of the movie  
• ratings.movie_id: to link ratings back to a film  
• ratings.avg_rating: to decide whether the movie’s rating is above 8 (condition: avg_rating > 8)  
• director_mapping.movie_id: to know which movies each director worked on  
• director_mapping.name_id: director’s identifier that we will later translate to the actual name  
• names.id: primary key that matches director_mapping.name_id  
• names.name: human‑readable director name we finally want to show  

Principal filter / join conditions we will need  

1. ratings.avg_rating > 8                                -- keep only high‑rated films  
2. ratings.movie_id = genre.movie_id              -- to attach genres  
3. ratings.movie_id = director_mapping.movie_id   -- to attach directors  
4. director_mapping.name_id = names.id            -- to get the director’s name  
5. genre.genre IN (top‑3 subquery)                 -- keep only the most frequent high‑rated genres  

Below are ten exploratory SQL queries (each capped with LIMIT 20) that progress from simple inspection to the final answer.

```sql
-- 1. Peek at a few movies that have an average rating above 8
SELECT DISTINCT "movie_id", "avg_rating"
FROM "ratings"
WHERE "avg_rating" > 8
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. See which genres those highly rated movies belong to
SELECT DISTINCT r."movie_id", g."genre"
FROM "ratings" AS r
JOIN "genre"  AS g ON r."movie_id" = g."movie_id"
WHERE r."avg_rating" > 8
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Count how many high‑rated movies fall into each genre
SELECT g."genre", COUNT(*) AS "high_rated_cnt"
FROM "ratings" AS r
JOIN "genre"  AS g ON r."movie_id" = g."movie_id"
WHERE r."avg_rating" > 8
GROUP BY g."genre"
ORDER BY "high_rated_cnt" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Retrieve the top three genres with the greatest number of >8‑rated movies
SELECT g."genre", COUNT(*) AS "high_rated_cnt"
FROM "ratings" AS r
JOIN "genre"  AS g ON r."movie_id" = g."movie_id"
WHERE r."avg_rating" > 8
GROUP BY g."genre"
ORDER BY "high_rated_cnt" DESC
LIMIT 3;
```

```sql
-- 5. List the directors (name_id only) of movies rated above 8
SELECT DISTINCT d."name_id", r."movie_id"
FROM "ratings"          AS r
JOIN "director_mapping" AS d ON r."movie_id" = d."movie_id"
WHERE r."avg_rating" > 8
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Attach the actual director names
SELECT DISTINCT n."name", d."movie_id"
FROM "ratings"          AS r
JOIN "director_mapping" AS d ON r."movie_id" = d."movie_id"
JOIN "names"            AS n ON d."name_id"  = n."id"
WHERE r."avg_rating" > 8
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Restrict directors to movies in only the previously identified top‑three genres
SELECT DISTINCT n."name", d."movie_id", g."genre"
FROM "ratings"          AS r
JOIN "genre"            AS g ON r."movie_id" = g."movie_id"
JOIN "director_mapping" AS d ON r."movie_id" = d."movie_id"
JOIN "names"            AS n ON d."name_id"  = n."id"
WHERE r."avg_rating" > 8
  AND g."genre" IN (
        SELECT g2."genre"
        FROM "ratings" AS r2
        JOIN "genre"   AS g2 ON r2."movie_id" = g2."movie_id"
        WHERE r2."avg_rating" > 8
        GROUP BY g2."genre"
        ORDER BY COUNT(*) DESC
        LIMIT 3
  )
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Count high‑rated (>8) movies per director but only inside the top‑three genres
SELECT n."name",
       COUNT(*) AS "high_rated_movies_in_top_genres"
FROM "ratings"          AS r
JOIN "genre"            AS g ON r."movie_id" = g."movie_id"
JOIN "director_mapping" AS d ON r."movie_id" = d."movie_id"
JOIN "names"            AS n ON d."name_id"  = n."id"
WHERE r."avg_rating" > 8
  AND g."genre" IN (
        SELECT g2."genre"
        FROM "ratings" AS r2
        JOIN "genre"   AS g2 ON r2."movie_id" = g2."movie_id"
        WHERE r2."avg_rating" > 8
        GROUP BY g2."genre"
        ORDER BY COUNT(*) DESC
        LIMIT 3
  )
GROUP BY n."name"
ORDER BY "high_rated_movies_in_top_genres" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Select the top four directors with the most high‑rated movies within those genres
SELECT n."name",
       COUNT(*) AS "high_rated_movies_in_top_genres"
FROM "ratings"          AS r
JOIN "genre"            AS g ON r."movie_id" = g."movie_id"
JOIN "director_mapping" AS d ON r."movie_id" = d."movie_id"
